Strictly speaking this should check for overflow, and because bubblewrap is sometimes setuid, I'm going to be strict about this. I know that you're only allowing overlayfs in the non-setuid case, but once this function exists, it would be very easy for someone to start using it in a security-critical code path.

Something like this (untested):

```suggestion
  size_t needed;
  size_t wanted;
  
  if (!__builtin_add_overflow (dest->offset, len + 1, &needed))
    die_oom ();

  if (needed > dest->size)
    {
      if (!__builtin_mul_overflow (needed, 2, &wanted))
        die_oom ();

      dest->str = xrealloc (dest->str, wanted);
      dest->size = wanted;
    }
```

